<p>A fire at an auto parts factory in Daejeon, South Korea, killed at least 14 people and injured nearly 60 others after breaking out around lunchtime on Friday. Officials believe about 170 workers were at the site when the blaze began. Several reports said some workers jumped from windows to escape as thick smoke and flames spread quickly through the three-storey building. By Saturday, firefighters had recovered bodies from the charred wreckage and said they had accounted for everyone previously listed as missing, while rescue crews kept searching under dangerous conditions because of collapse risks and hazardous materials stored at the plant. Authorities had not announced a cause, though witnesses cited in local reporting said they heard an explosion before the fire spread rapidly. President Lee Jae Myung ordered officials to mobilize all available personnel and equipment for the rescue, underscoring the seriousness of one of South Korea’s deadliest factory fires in recent years.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vyml0VKtqu1IeJR-Cn3y2q4AkZf_raamzwrWW8LmXy1Wq41GpHLmBp5pJETa3MwpavQSO4rr8na2-qMD2AWd4yKO5UVVdKStmlOAHBYGwHWu' alt='Smoke rises from a car parts factory in Daejeon, South Korea, on March 20, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Injury toll: Fire authorities said 25 people were seriously injured and about 34 to 35 others suffered less serious injuries. Twenty-eight people were taken to hospital, and four underwent surgery for broken bones and other injuries.</li><li>Fire duration: The blaze broke out at about 1 p.m. on Friday and was contained by 11:48 p.m., showing how long crews fought the fire before they could safely enter the wreckage.</li><li>Hazard challenge: Rescue efforts slowed because sodium stored at the site could explode if handled improperly, adding another layer of danger to the firefighting operation.</li><li>Recent precedent: The fire is the deadliest factory blaze in South Korea in two years, following the 2024 Aricell battery factory disaster that killed 22 people.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Lee Jae Myung: Lee ordered officials to mobilize all available resources, including personnel and equipment, for rescue operations at the site. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1984226/11-dead-dozens-injured-in-south-korea-car-plant-fire'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Fire authorities: Firefighters treated the structure as unstable and finished searching the wreckage before confirming that all previously missing people had been accounted for. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/21/south-korea-fire-daejeon-car-parts-factory'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Witnesses cited by Yonhap: One witness said they heard an explosion before the fire spread, an early detail investigators may examine as they work to determine the cause. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1984226/11-dead-dozens-injured-in-south-korea-car-plant-fire'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-blaze-at-auto-parts-factory-kills-11/a-76448240'>South Korea: Blaze at auto parts factory kills 11</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/south-korea-car-plant-fire-many-killed-march-21-2026/article70767397.ece'>At least 11 killed in South Korea car plant fire</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/20/world/asia/south-korea-factory-fire-deaths.html'>​At Least 14 Killed in South Korean Factory Fire</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/videos/c87wg74wlgyo'>Watch: Thick smoke billows from South Korea car parts plant in deadly fire</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/officials-10-people-killed-south-korean-factory-fire-131270544'>Officials say at least 10 people were killed in a South Korean factory fire</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/21/south-korea-fire-daejeon-car-parts-factory'>At least 14 people killed in f